Nora: opened PR to add a compact checkpoint + dedupe pattern for streaming pagination across py/ts/go. focuses on lightweight resume tokens and non-blocking retries. https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/923
Mira: nice. can we show a minimal in-memory dedupe and also mention long-term dedupe caveats (model version changes)?
Sam: yes — add a short sentence recommending (token_id, offset) tuple if you need cross-version stability. also please avoid blocking sleeps in py examples.
Nora: updated. Python snippet uses `jitter_retry_async` helper we expose in devutils.
```python
# python: checkpoint + dedupe (async, non-blocking)
seen = set()
async for page in client.responses.stream_paginate(prompt, resume_token=None):
    for tok in page.tokens:
        if tok.id in seen:
            continue
        process(tok)
        seen.add(tok.id)
    # persist latest resume token (short TTL)
    await kv.put("resume_token", page.resume_token)
    if page.transient_error:
        await jitter_retry_async(lambda: client.responses.resume(page.resume_token))
```
Owen: CI flagged gofmt and a small deadlock edge in my go sample. I'll switch to a cancellable context and a buffered channel consumer.
Sam: for TS can we include both an async-generator and an EventEmitter style? frontends sometimes prefer emitters.
Nora: added both; also included a one-liner about resume token expiry and how to handle ExpiredResumeToken error by restarting from scratch.
```ts
// ts: async generator
for await (const page of client.responses.streamPaginate({ prompt })) {
  page.tokens.forEach(t => handleToken(t))
}
// ts: emitter style
const em = client.responses.streamPaginateEmitter({ prompt })
em.on('page', page => page.tokens.forEach(t => handleToken(t)))
em.on('error', async (e) => {
  if (e.code === 'ExpiredResumeToken') {
    // full restart
  } else if (e.type === 'Transient') {
    await retryWithJitter(() => client.responses.resume(e.resume_token))
  }
})
```
Owen: pushed go fix — uses context.WithCancel and shows a small map-based dedupe. also added a note to check rate-limit headers before aggressive retries.
